# .gitignore for the Figure 2C analysis.
#
# The plotting notebook (Fig2C.ipynb), the exploratory notebook
# (fig_infecting_different_orgs.ipynb), the host-classification script
# (host_to_tax_id.py) and the rendered figure
# (prokaryote_vs_eukaryote_infecting_viruses_AFPP.pdf) are tracked. Every data
# table they read or write now lives in data/viral_proteomes/ at the top of the
# repository (see the README there); the rules below only keep stray local
# copies of them out of this directory.

# --- Stray copies of the data tables (the real ones are in data/viral_proteomes/) -
# Third-party downloads:
#   virushostdb.tsv               Virus-Host DB (https://www.genome.jp/virushostdb/)
#   org_id_to_proteome_id.tsv     UniProt proteome-ID <-> organism-ID map
# Upstream prediction output:
#   viral_proteome_fraction_disorder_by_prot_and_total_proteome.tsv
# Regenerated locally by host_to_tax_id.py:
#   archaeal_infecting_viruses.tsv, bacterial_infecting_viruses.tsv,
#   ecoli_infecting_viruses.tsv, eukaryotic_infecting_viruses.tsv,
#   human_infecting_viruses.tsv
# Catch-all so any additional data tables dropped in here stay untracked.
*.tsv

# --- Jupyter / Python cruft -------------------------------------------------------
.ipynb_checkpoints/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.pytest_cache/

# --- OS / editor cruft ------------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
.DS_Store?
._*
.Spotlight-V100
.Trashes
Thumbs.db
ehthumbs.db
Desktop.ini
*~
*.swp
*.swo
.idea/
.vscode/
